/* 
LeetCode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/monthly-transactions-i/

Problem Name: Monthly Transactions I

Beginner-Friendly Explanation:
We need to calculate statistics for transactions grouped by month and country:
1. Total number of transactions (trans_count).
2. Total transaction amount (trans_total_amount).
3. Number of approved transactions (approved_count).
4. Total approved transaction amount (approved_total_amount).

Step-by-Step Approach:
1. Extract month in YYYY-MM format using DATE_FORMAT(trans_date, '%Y-%m').
2. COUNT(id) → gives the total number of transactions for that group.
3. SUM(amount) → gives the total money transacted in that group.
4. To calculate approved-only stats:
   - Option 1 (using SUM):
       • SUM(IF(state='approved',1,0)) → adds 1 for approved, 0 for others → approved count.
       • SUM(IF(state='approved',amount,0)) → adds amount only if approved → approved sum.
   - Option 2 (using COUNT):
       • COUNT(IF(state='approved',1,NULL)) → counts only approved rows.
       • SUM(IF(state='approved',amount,0)) → same as above for approved amounts.
5. GROUP BY month and country to compute results for each combination.

Why JOIN is NOT needed here:
- All required fields (state, amount, date, country) are in one table (Transactions).
- No relationship with another table exists, so JOIN is unnecessary.

Input Example:
Transactions table:
+------+---------+----------+--------+------------+
| id   | country | state    | amount | trans_date |
+------+---------+----------+--------+------------+
| 121  | US      | approved | 1000   | 2018-12-18 |
| 122  | US      | declined | 2000   | 2018-12-19 |
| 123  | US      | approved | 2000   | 2019-01-01 |
| 124  | DE      | approved | 2000   | 2019-01-07 |
+------+---------+----------+--------+------------+

Output:
+----------+---------+-------------+----------------+--------------------+-----------------------+
| month    | country | trans_count | approved_count | trans_total_amount | approved_total_amount |
+----------+---------+-------------+----------------+--------------------+-----------------------+
| 2018-12  | US      | 2           | 1              | 3000               | 1000                  |
| 2019-01  | US      | 1           | 1              | 2000               | 2000                  |
| 2019-01  | DE      | 1           | 1              | 2000               | 2000                  |
+----------+---------+-------------+----------------+--------------------+-----------------------+

Explanation:
- For 2018-12 & US: 2 transactions, 1 approved → total 3000, approved 1000.
- For 2019-01 & US: 1 transaction, approved → total 2000, approved 2000.
- For 2019-01 & DE: 1 transaction, approved → total 2000, approved 2000.

-------------------------------------------
SQL Solution 1 (Using SUM(IF(...))):
-------------------------------------------
*/
SELECT DATE_FORMAT(trans_date, '%Y-%m') AS month,
       country,
       COUNT(id) AS trans_count, -- total number of transactions
       SUM(IF(state='approved', 1, 0)) AS approved_count, -- add 1 for approved, 0 otherwise
       SUM(amount) AS trans_total_amount, -- sum of all transaction amounts
       SUM(IF(state='approved', amount, 0)) AS approved_total_amount -- sum only approved amounts
FROM Transactions
GROUP BY DATE_FORMAT(trans_date, '%Y-%m'), country;


-------------------------------------------
/* 
SQL Solution 2 (Using COUNT(IF(...))):
Same logic, but use COUNT with a NULL trick for approved_count.
*/
-------------------------------------------
SELECT DATE_FORMAT(trans_date, '%Y-%m') AS month,
       country,
       COUNT(id) AS trans_count, -- total number of transactions
       COUNT(IF(state='approved', 1, NULL)) AS approved_count, -- count only approved rows
       SUM(amount) AS trans_total_amount, -- sum of all amounts
       SUM(IF(state='approved', amount, 0)) AS approved_total_amount -- sum only approved amounts
FROM Transactions
GROUP BY DATE_FORMAT(trans_date, '%Y-%m'), country;
